      "citations": null,
      "text": "This builds SMB from the value-weighted 2x3 size/book-to-market portfolios, following Ken French's method: SMB is the simple average of the three small-cap portfolio returns minus the simple average of the three big-cap portfolio returns. Only the first (value-weighted monthly) block is parsed, and rows with missing portfolio data are skipped.\n\n```python\nimport re\nimport csv\n\nINFILE = \"6_Portfolios_2x3.csv\"\nOUTFILE = \"output.csv\"\n\nMISSING_VALUES = (-99.99, -999.0)\n\n\ndef is_missing(v):\n    return any(abs(v - m) < 1e-9 for m in MISSING_VALUES)\n\n\ndef parse_value_weighted_monthly(path):\n    \"\"\"\n    Parse the first monthly block (Average Value Weighted Returns -- Monthly).\n    Returns list of (yyyymm:int, [six floats or None]).\n    \"\"\"\n    date_re = re.compile(r\"^\\s*(\\d{6})\\s*,(.*)$\")\n    rows = []\n    started = False\n    with open(path, \"r\", encoding=\"latin-1\") as f:\n        for line in f:\n            s = line.strip()\n            m = date_re.match(s)\n            if m:\n                started = True\n                parts = [p.strip() for p in m.group(2).split(\",\")]\n                if len(parts) < 6:\n                    continue\n                vals = []\n                for p in parts[:6]:\n                    try:\n                        v = float(p)\n                    except ValueError:\n                        vals.append(None)\n                        continue\n                    if is_missing(v):\n                        vals.append(None)\n                    else:\n                        vals.append(v)\n                rows.append((int(m.group(1)), vals))\n            else:\n                # End of the contiguous monthly value-weighted block\n                if started:\n                    break\n    return rows\n\n\ndef main():\n    rows = parse_value_weighted_monthly(INFILE)\n\n    out = []\n    seen = set()\n    for date, vals in rows:\n        if date in seen:\n            continue\n        seen.add(date)\n        if any(v is None for v in vals):\n            continue\n        # Columns: SMALL LoBM, ME1 BM2, SMALL HiBM, BIG LoBM, ME2 BM2, BIG HiBM\n        small = (vals[0] + vals[1] + vals[2]) / 3.0\n        big = (vals[3] + vals[4] + vals[5]) / 3.0\n        out.append((date, small - big))\n\n    out.sort(key=lambda x: x[0])\n\n    with open(OUTFILE, \"w\", newline=\"\") as f:\n        w = csv.writer(f)\n        w.writerow([\"date\", \"value\"])\n        for date, val in out:\n            w.writerow([date, repr(float(val))])\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```",
      "type": "text"
    }
